#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""capri-watch: event hooks that wake Capri.

One small poller per machine. It watches GitHub (bella only), the local Synaps daemon's
sessions, failed systemd units, free disk, the Jawz backup and a few opt-in extras, and
delivers each new event into Capri's session as ONE short framed line:

    [watch] <event>@<host>: <what> (<id/link>)

bella delivers with `synaps send --session capri --source watch:<event> -- <line>`; avante runs
the same command on bella over ssh (BatchMode). The transport is pluggable ([deliver] transport
= "local" | "ssh" | "command"), so agent-comms can replace ssh later.

Safeguards: dedupe (an event fires once per state change), burst bundling (one digest per
`bundle_s` window), a wake cap per hour, her DND and music state (read from the avatar's control
socket, the one capri-ctl talks to), quiet hours, stale held events dropped (a dropped condition
is re-checked). Her own session is never reported (no loops); sessions are never attached to.

Config: ~/.config/synaps-avatar/watch.toml (tools/capri-watch/watch.toml is the documented
example; a missing file means the built-in defaults below). State: ~/.local/state/capri-watch/.

  capri-watch                  run (the systemd --user unit)
  capri-watch --dry-run        print what would be sent; never sends, never writes state
  capri-watch --once           one poll pass, flush at once, exit
  capri-watch --print-config   the merged config as JSON
"""
